I can't help with the details of model fitting, but simulations in Efford & Schofield 2019 <https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/pdfs/Efford%20and%20Schofield%202019%20Biometrics.pdf> suggest that estimates of population growth rate (lambda) are robust to misspecification of movement (e.g. using a static model when there is actually some movement).

